<title>UK: UK net consumer credit up 780 mln stg in March.</title>
<headline>UK net consumer credit up 780 mln stg in March.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England released the</p>
<p>following seasonally adjusted consumer credit data -</p>
<p>NET LENDING (previously released data in brackets, in million stg)</p>
<p>					     MARCH   FEBRUARY	MAR,96</p>
<p> Total net lending		     2,550   3,065 (3,054)  2,295</p>
<p>  -- Consumer credit		     780   1,192 (1,221)    851</p>
<p>  -- Secured on dwellings	    1,770   1,872 (1,833)  1,444</p>
<p>BREAKDOWN of net consumer lending BY SOURCE -</p>
<p>  -- Banks				 570    981    (994)	664</p>
<p>  -- Building societies		  8     30    (31)	  63</p>
<p>  -- Other specialist lenders	169    194    (198)	117</p>
<p>  -- Retailers			    44	6    (4)	    6</p>
<p>  -- Insurance companies	     -11    -19    (-6)	   1</p>
<p>  -- Credit card			 205    337    (337)	205</p>
<p>CONSUMER CREDIT (seasonally adjusted, in PCT)</p>
<p> Total personal borrowing mth/mth  0.5    0.6   (0.6)	0.5</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;    annualised 3mth    7.1    7.2   (7.2)	5.7</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;	  &quot;     yr/yr    6.9    6.8   (6.9)	5.2</p>
<p> Consumer credit mth/mth	     1.0    1.6   (1.6)	1.3</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;    annualised 3mth   16.0   17.3   (17.9)    14.1</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;     yr/yr		17.1   17.4   (17.5)    13.4</p>
<p> Secured on dwellings mth/mth	0.4    0.5   ( 0.4)     0.4</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;    annualised 3mth    5.6    5.4   ( 5.4)     4.3</p>
<p>   &quot;	 &quot;     yr/yr		 5.1    5.1   ( 5.1)     3.9</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
</text>
